    edMeta: '( Where it fits )',
    edH: 'Catalog photography: clarity that closes the sale.',
    edSub: 'The clean product pages your shop and marketplaces run on.',
    whatH: 'What it is',
    whatP: [
      "Catalog photography is the straight, clean product imagery a shopper judges the product by — front, back, a detail close-up and one on-model shot, all on a consistent background. It isn’t there to set a mood; it’s there to show exactly what someone is buying, with nothing left to guess.",
      // Was drie zinnen. Het beeld erboven laat nu zien wat ze uitlegden.
      'The picture above is the whole argument: shot the same way end to end, a range reads as one considered line instead of a pile of separate photos. That is what makes a small brand look established.',
